# The CFD solve screens: a solve in progress, cancelled with its solved points on offer, finished, the 3D stability solve in
# progress and finished. A real solve takes minutes and the driver waits for running tasks, so the solves are scripted
# (`analyze/solve_demo.rs`: the same events the worker sends, made-up numbers; the real stream is covered by the ignored tests
# of `analyze/cfd.rs`):
#   BOWSHOCK_CFD_DEMO=mid,done,lift-mid,lift-done cargo run -q -p bowshock -- drive --example crates/bowshock/scripts/cfd-progress.drive out/cfd-progress
viewport 1300x800
click "Analyze"
click "CFD table"
move (100, 700)
move (102, 702)
screenshot solve-mid-dark.png

# Cancel with four points solved: the points are on offer.
click "Cancel"
move (100, 700)
move (102, 702)
screenshot solve-stopped-dark.png
click "Discard"

# A whole solve, finished: the summary row.
click "Re-solve"
move (100, 700)
move (102, 702)
screenshot solve-done-dark.png

# The 3D stability solve in progress and finished.
click "Solve stability (3D)"
move (100, 700)
move (102, 702)
screenshot solve-3d-mid-dark.png
click "Cancel"
click "Solve stability (3D)"
move (100, 700)
move (102, 702)
screenshot solve-3d-done-dark.png

# The same mid-solve screen in the light theme.
click "Re-solve"
click "Prefs"
click "Light"
click "Done"
move (100, 700)
move (102, 702)
screenshot solve-mid-light.png
